  "id": "COMPOUND:18043 - PROTEIN:5798",
  "verbalization": "Arjunglucoside I is implicated in the biological pathway leading to NH-6 through a series of target interactions. The evidence suggests that Arjunglucoside I acts as a target for multiple entities, including Hepatocyte and VMRC-LCP, which in turn target NH-6. This indicates a potential mechanism where Arjunglucoside I may influence the activity of these intermediaries, ultimately affecting NH-6. The shared involvement of Hepatocyte and VMRC-LCP in the pathway suggests a possible role for Arjunglucoside I in modulating cellular processes that are relevant to NH-6. The integration of these targets highlights a possible dependency on metabolic or signaling pathways that are central to the function of NH-6. The evidence supports a mechanism where Arjunglucoside I may act as a modulator of these pathways, potentially influencing NH-6 through a series of intermediate targets.",
